## Autonomous execution (overnight / watchdog)

This repo is set up to be driven autonomously by Claude Code, sprint by sprint. The autonomous-execution docs live in `docs/develop/`:

- `docs/develop/AGENT_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL.md` — the operating loop (how to consume the plan and execute safely).
- `docs/develop/SPRINTS.md` — the plan (sprints → batches → tasks → acceptance).
- `docs/develop/ROADMAP.md` — high-level sprint sequence; `PRODUCT.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` / `DECISIONS.md` / `TESTING.md` — operational summaries.
- `docs/develop/AGENT_PROGRESS.md` — the handoff log; update after every meaningful step.
- `.claude/agents/` (`sprint-runner`, `code-reviewer`, `test-engineer`, `architect-reviewer`) and `.claude/skills/` (`execute-sprint`, `verify-feature`, `update-progress`, `debug-failure`).
- `scripts/claude-night-runner.ps1` — Windows watchdog that resumes the run every 30 min.

To run autonomously, read `docs/develop/AGENT_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL.md` first. The same safety gates apply: work on `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}` branches only, never push to `main`/`develop`, never deploy or run destructive DB ops without human approval.

## When working here

- Read the source docs for the exact spec of whatever module/flow you touch; they are detailed.
- Confirm a change is inside the documented MVP scope before building it.
- Keep high-risk actions behind human approval. When in doubt, generate a draft + create a question / approval gate rather than acting.
- Communicate with the user in their language; keep code, identifiers and docs in English.
